  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Montana received $928M in federal contract obligations in FY2026 to date. The state recorded 5,997 awards with an average award size of $155K. Obligations fell 19.1% year over year. Fiscal-year comparisons show obligations of $691M in FY21, $925M in FY22, $1B in FY23, $1.1B in FY24, $1.1B in FY25, and $928M in FY26. The Department of Defense obligated $322M in Montana, followed by the Department of Agriculture with $228M and the Department of Homeland Security with $170M. S & K SECURITY GROUP LLC is the largest vendor by obligations at $135M, with ARCHER WESTERN FEDERAL JV at $58.8M and PAF ELECTRICAL, INC. at $57M. Nonscheduled Chartered Freight Air Transportation is the top NAICS industry at $142M, followed by Electronic and Precision Equipment Repair and Maintenance at $137M and Commercial and Institutional Building Construction at $119M. All figures are contract obligations and current-year totals are partial. This snapshot shows which agencies, vendors, and industries are dominating federal spending in Montana through the FY2026 fiscal year to date.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "How did obligations change year over year?",
        "body": "Montana obligations fell 19.1% year over year. Obligations by fiscal year were $691M in FY21, $925M in FY22, $1B in FY23, $1.1B in FY24, $1.1B in FY25, and $928M in FY26. The FY2026 total of $928M is a partial, fiscal year to date figure. The average award size for FY2026 to date is $155K across 5,997 awards."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Which agencies and vendors dominate FY2026 spending?",
        "body": "The Department of Defense obligated $322M in Montana in FY2026 to date. The Department of Agriculture obligated $228M, and the Department of Homeland Security obligated $170M. S & K SECURITY GROUP LLC received $135M, ARCHER WESTERN FEDERAL JV received $58.8M, and PAF ELECTRICAL, INC. received $57M in obligations."
      }
    ]
  },
